✓ Use intermediate and output directories that are on /share/apps
  Durrent dir structure:
    datadir: /share/apps/nsidc0802/nsidc0802/dev/scotts/

    TB fields drop-in-the-bucket gridded from L1R data:  [*** these are included in nsidc0802 netCDF file ***]
        {datadir}/tb_gw1am2_grd/{gridid}/{year}/{month}/tb_gw1am2_{gridid}_{chanres}_{ymd}.dat
      eg
        /share/apps/nsidc0802/nsidc0802/dev/scotts/tb_gw1am2_grd/psn25/2024/03/tb_gw1am2_psn25_h19r06_20240315.dat

    TB fields spatial-frequency-matched:
        {datadir}/tb_gw1am2_sfm/{gridid}/{year}/{month}/tb_gw1am2_{gridid}_{chanres}_{ymd}.dat
      eg
        /share/apps/nsidc0802/nsidc0802/dev/scotts/tb_gw1am2_sfm/psn25/2024/03/tb_gw1am2_psn25_h19r06_20240315.dat

    TB fields spatial-frequency-matched and with linear regression applied:  [*** these are included in nsidc0802 netCDF file ***]
      ie "calibrated"
        {datadir}/tb_gw1am2_cal/{gridid}/{year}/{month}/tb_gw1am2_{gridid}_{chanres}_{ymd}.dat
      eg
        /share/apps/nsidc0802/nsidc0802/dev/scotts/tb_gw1am2_cal/psn25/2024/03/tb_gw1am2_psn25_h19r06_20240315.dat

  - Note: these should probably be dev-dependent so they are user-independent
  - Note: Directly-gridded files will not change unless the gridding
     methodology changes
     - But, sfmlr (spatial frequency matched, linearly regressed) files
       *will* change until the sfm/lr coefficients are finalized

✓ Remove code that generates unnecessary gridded TB fields

